  "descriptionKey": "- Revenue passenger-kilometres measure total passenger traffic by air.\n- One revenue passenger-kilometre equals one paying passenger traveling one kilometre.\n- A flight carrying 150 paying passengers over 1,000 kilometres generates 150,000 revenue passenger-kilometres.\n- This metric combines passenger numbers and distances traveled, so it is more informative than passenger counts alone.\n- It is not a simple count of passengers: long-distance travel contributes more than short-distance travel.",
